note S4 part (spec 6): parts of a local (an edit), of an unsized edit, of an unsized view and of a
note text; `view part` of an edit; an empty part at the end; a part passed to an inline function; o and k
note from calls. The callee sees len = k and elements o .. o+k-1. Exit 0 when every check holds.
om2
text msg "0123456789"
fn plen v view uchar * to ulong
ret len v
end
fn first v view uchar * to ulong
ret ulong get v 0
end
fn fill e edit uchar * c uchar to ulong
for i ulong len e
put e i c
end
ret add plen view part e 1 1 len e
end
fn ifirst v view uchar * to ulong inline
ret ulong get v 0
end
fn sub2 v view uchar * o ulong to ulong
ret first part v o 2
end
fn two to ulong
ret 2
end
fn main to int
a = new uchar 10 46
if ne fill part a 3 4 88 5
ret 1
end
if ne get a 2 46
ret 2
end
if ne get a 6 88
ret 3
end
if ne get a 7 46
ret 4
end
if ne first part msg 7 3 55
ret 5
end
if ne sub2 msg 4 52
ret 6
end
if ne plen part a 10 0 0
ret 7
end
if ne ifirst part msg 9 1 57
ret 8
end
if ne plen part a two add two 1 3
ret 9
end
if ne ifirst view part a 6 two 88
ret 10
end
ret 0
end
